This example is only to show you the basic layout of a Global Plugin.</p>
<p>Copy and paste the code between (but not including) the start and end ma=
rkers into a new text file with a name of example2.py, which should be save=
d in the globalPlugins subdirectory.
Be very careful to keep all tabs and spaces intact.</p>
<p>Once saved in the right place, either restart NVDA or choose Reload Plug=
ins found under Tools in the NVDA menu.</p>
<p>From anywhere, you can now press <code>NVDA+shift+v</code> to have NVDA'=
s version spoken and brailled.</p>
