<p>This Global Plugin file starts with two comment lines, which describe wh=
at the file is for.</p>
<p>It then imports the globalPluginHandler module, so that the Global Plugi=
n has access to the base GlobalPlugin class.</p>
<p>It also imports a few other modules, namely ui, buildVersion and scriptH=
andler, which this specific plugin needs in order for it to perform the nec=
essary actions to announce the version.</p>
<p>Next, it defines a class called GlobalPlugin, which is inherited from gl=
obalPluginHandler.GlobalPlugin.</p>
